{
  "name": "shops",
  "about": "A town whose Merchant is a master (level 5) deals with the vendors its host counts: a buying vendor is a standing order the Merchant fills a lot a day from its warehouse (OrderFilled names the vendor, for the host to put the goods in and take the spurs off its card), a selling vendor is bought from for the order's goods (StallBought: the goods out of the vendor, the spurs paid into it), and a vendor touching the desk is the town's own, shown what the Merchant lists (Shelf) and counted again with a lot bought and its coin collected. A vendor put up for the town's board is paid for; a deed shop for a rent that isn't there is refused. What the screens show comes from Shops and Deeds. Saved and loaded, the shops are as they were; a vendor broken takes its shop with it.",
